    "intro_html":  "Jerk chicken and cold mango salsa is one of the great flavor pairings, sweet and fiery in the same bite. We marinate skinless thigh in a jerk-spiced mix of citrus, soy and a little brown sugar and honey, tuck it into a wrap with a modest scoop of rice and kidney beans, and top it with a fresh mango, tomato and red onion salsa. It is the only Caribbean plate in this batch, and every burrito still lands \u003cstrong\u003eunder 400 calories with 4 ounces of meat\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e, on a high fiber tortilla that keeps you near 5 grams of net carb. We have a One Pot Caribbean Jerk Chicken and Rice on the site; this is the marinated, hand-held version finished with a bright salsa instead of a baked rice pot.",
