    "shop_smart":  [
                       "Skinless thigh is cheaper than breast, stays juicy through reheating, and is the right cut for jerk. Buy the family pack and freeze the extra.",
                       "One ripe mango does the salsa. Buy it a few days ahead and let it soften on the counter so it dices sweet instead of sour.",
                       "Jerk seasoning in a jar keeps for a long time and seasons several batches, so buy it once and let it work.",
                       "Kidney beans and rice are the cheap ballast that make this filling, and both store in the pantry indefinitely, so buy the bigger sizes."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Whisk the orange juice, soy sauce, brown sugar, honey, jerk seasoning and salt into a marinade. Add the skinless chicken thighs and let them sit at least 30 minutes.",
                    "Cook the rice until tender and set it aside, and warm the drained kidney beans.",
                    "Grill or sear the marinated thighs until charred at the edges and cooked through, then chop them.",
                    "Make the salsa by tossing the diced mango, halved cherry tomatoes and diced red onion with the lime juice and chopped cilantro.",
                    "Lay a small bed of rice and beans down each tortilla, add a share of the jerk chicken, a spoon of Greek yogurt and a light dusting of reduced fat mozzarella, then top with the mango salsa.",
                    "Weigh the rice, beans and chicken together, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14 so each burrito gets the same base before you add the salsa.",
                    "Fold in the sides, roll tight, wrap each one, and portion into 14 containers."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "Weigh the rice, beans and chicken, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14 so the calorie count actually holds across all 14. Add the salsa and the spoon of yogurt on top, then roll. Each burrito carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e. Keep the salsa in a separate cup if you are freezing these, and add it fresh after reheating.",
